---
import { readdir } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { runStore } from '../lib/run-store';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Dataset from '../components/Dataset.astro';
import Table from '../components/Table.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { getReports } from '../lib/reports';
import { dataset } from '../lib/pingstore';

const index = await runStore.index();
const reports = new Map((await getReports()).map(report => [report.data.id, report]));
const experiments = (await readdir('../experiments', { withFileTypes: true }))
  .filter(entry => entry.isDirectory() && /^exp\d+$/.test(entry.name))
  .map(entry => entry.name)
  .sort((a, b) => b.localeCompare(a, 'en', { numeric: true }));
const inventories = await Promise.all(experiments.map(async experiment => {
  const report = reports.get(experiment);
  const inputs = [...new Set([experiment, ...(report?.data.inputs ?? [])])];
  try {
    let datasets = await Promise.all(inputs.map(id => dataset(id)));
    // A report without data does not claim these historical runs as evidence.
    if (!report?.data.tags.includes('data')) {
      datasets = datasets.map(data => ({ ...data,
        runs: data.runs.map(run => ({ ...run, selected: false, used: false })),
      }));
    }
    return { experiment, report, datasets, error: undefined };
  } catch (error) {
    return { experiment, report, datasets: undefined,
      error: (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code === 'ENOENT'
        ? 'A selected run or recorded input is missing from local Pingstore and R2.'
        : 'The run inventory could not be read. Check the run records.' };
  }
}));
const completedRuns = Object.keys(index.runs);
const currentRuns = completedRuns.filter(id => index.runs[id].status === 'Current').length;
const requiredRuns = completedRuns.filter(id => index.runs[id].status === 'Required').length;
const unusedRuns = completedRuns.filter(id => index.runs[id].status === 'Unused').length;
const unresolvedRuns = completedRuns.filter(id => index.runs[id].status === 'Unresolved').length;
const unavailableExperiments = inventories.filter(inventory => inventory.error).length;
const pruneCommands = `uv run pingstore evict --all --dry-run

# After reviewing the plan, replace PLAN_HASH with its complete sha256 hash.
uv run pingstore evict --all --confirm PLAN_HASH`;
---

<Page title="Pingstore" description="Dataset tables for Pinglab experiments." noindex>
  <d-title>
    <h1>Pingstore</h1>
  </d-title>
  <d-article role="article" aria-label="Pingstore">
    <p>The appendix lists the available local and R2 run inventory for each experiment, newest experiment first. “Current” marks the current presentation and its exact input ancestry. Storage is separate from the machine where a run executed. Historical holdings remain unresolved until active publication evidence has been established; unused identifies history with no retention root in the resolved context.</p>
    <Table headers={['Total holdings', 'Current', 'Required', 'Unused', 'Unresolved']}
      rows={[[completedRuns.length, currentRuns, requiredRuns, unusedRuns, unresolvedRuns]]} label="Run totals" />
    {index.operation && <p role="status">An unfinished {index.operation.kind} operation retains evidence: {index.operation.plan_hash}. Resume its original verified plan before starting another cleanup.</p>}
    {(index.publication_unavailable?.length ?? 0) > 0 && <p role="status">Availability of {index.publication_unavailable!.length} published runs is unresolved in this source context.</p>}
    <p>Counts include each holding once. Unresolved holdings are not classified as unused.
      {unavailableExperiments > 0 && <> Dataset details for {unavailableExperiments} experiments could not be resolved.</>}
    </p>
    {completedRuns.filter(id => !index.runs[id].record).map(id => <p role="status">{id}: {index.runs[id].unresolved.join('; ')}</p>)}
    <p>To free local disk space, evict verified backup copies with these commands from the repository root. Review the dry-run plan before confirming. Report-used runs remain readable from R2; protected runs and inputs needed by unfinished work stay local. Confirmation verifies remote bytes before deleting any local copies.</p>
    <Code code={pruneCommands} lang="sh" />
  </d-article>
  <d-appendix distill-prerendered aria-label="Pingstore appendix">
    {inventories.map(({ experiment, report, datasets, error }) => <>
      <h2 id={experiment}>
        {report ? <a href={`/${experiment}`}>{experiment} — {report.data.title}</a> : experiment}
      </h2>
      <!-- Missing selected evidence stays unavailable; never substitute another run. -->
      {error ? <>
        <h3 id={`${experiment}-dataset`}>Dataset</h3>
        <section aria-labelledby={`${experiment}-dataset`}><p role="status">Dataset unavailable: {error}</p></section>
      </> : <Dataset experiment={experiment} datasets={datasets} headingId={`${experiment}-dataset`} />}
    </>)}
    {experiments.length === 0 && <p>No experiments are available.</p>}
  </d-appendix>
</Page>

<style>
  d-appendix { background: var(--surface); color: rgb(var(--ink) / .65); }
  d-appendix h2 { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 2rem 0 0; scroll-margin-top: 24px; }
  d-appendix h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  d-appendix section { min-width: 0; }
  @media print { d-appendix { background: white; } }
</style>
